// Sheet: "persistent AoE control zone, heavily obscuring gas; nauseating-
// condition rider (lose action on failed Constitution save)". No
// action-denial-on-failed-save primitive exists (no action-economy resource
// to deny in this real-time combat system, the same gap
// conjuration/hail_of_thorns.ron's own note already flags for a different
// rider). `BuffKind::Sickened` is the closest already-shipped analog for
// "nauseated" -- it's the same buff Necromancy's own ray_of_sickness.ron
// uses for the same real-world condition name, and its effects()
// (common/src/comp/buff.rs) bundle an accuracy penalty with a
// Bleeding-shaped HP-drain tick that can't be separated out. The sheet is
// explicit ("No damage") -- the strength here (0.2, well below
// ray_of_sickness.ron's already-mild 0.3 for a single 6s hit, applied here
// continuously for the whole zone duration instead) is kept deliberately low
// so the unavoidable drain reads as incidental nausea-flavor rather than a
// real damage source, closest available compromise rather than inventing a
// new BuffKind. `StaticAura` always places the zone at the caster's own
// position -- the sheet's 27 m cast range isn't mechanically expressed, same
// simplification as entangle/fog_cloud/grease.
StaticAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    energy_cost: 75.0,
    targets: OutOfGroup,
    auras: [
        (kind: Sickened, strength: 0.2, duration: Some(2), category: Some(Magical)),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(20.0),
    range: 6.0,
    sprite_info: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Conjuration), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
